# Wave T46 (Inglenook kit): giltfloor — Inglenook City's registered street kind (the fleet's street kinds carry the -floor suffix; the desire-path tiers key on it). WARM GILT SETTS: small rectangular stone setts in warm gold-ochre laid in a running offset grid, bronze grout lines, a fine sparkle fleck — the painting's warm paved streets and the town style line's gold. A SETT-GRID geometry: unlike Honeyfield's honeyfloor (hexagonal comb), Heritage's heritagefloor (large irregular flags), Coalseam's clinkerfloor (fine aggregate), Revelry's beamfloor (steel plates), Shingle's shellfloor (raked shell sand) and Clover's cloverfloor (flecked earth). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T46-INGLENOOK-PLAN.md §5.)
